 "Evaluate $(\\begin{aligned}36 \\\\ 33\\end{aligned}).$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that $(\\frac{36}{33})$ means the same thing as ${}_{36}{C}_{33}.$\n\n In general, the number of combinations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{C}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=36$ and $r=33,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{36}{C}_{33} & =\\frac{36!}{(36-33)!33!} \\\\  & =\\frac{36!}{3!33!} \\\\  & =\\frac{36\\cdot 35\\cdot 34\\cdot \\cancel{33!}}{3!\\cdot \\cancel{33!}} \\\\  & =\\frac{36\\cdot 35\\cdot 34}{3\\cdot 2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{42\\,840}{6} \\\\  & =7\\,140.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-85041/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6b720d4-59b0-5d86-b856-ff69abfe4152"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-85041"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-85044/selection/56e66b66988ed063c348f42210ea71f739de8db2bed4a9af7514491792cb1297" :answer/id #uuid "684f4154-590f-5a31-bdd3-df29b5d3c14b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\,480" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85044/selection/1b72553795d48e9e460a5278c4d8e5aa817a350c853cb8fc5d453121e55ea50f" :answer/id #uuid "869e351f-f79e-5549-a6e7-76e1f40e0275" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "19\\,380" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85044/selection/a444febd07c68eb775d52e9ee495ed7dd027664dbce304985f721bb26e2b1f78" :answer/id #uuid "149a1e67-016e-5a03-9fa8-7ed143111b4e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,860" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85044/selection/dbac2651a63793408ebec43c058d20d836a1a30dd12600da3020dd4d2c9a42a2" :answer/id #uuid "c51a0d43-908e-5439-ac81-3011e56a58c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9\\,280" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85044/selection/fd64b2f01b7996db4898da8b0692cf93293c961075f0931e716dcaafbc039a46" :answer/id #uuid "f3904f4a-2