by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{C}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $15$ questions, so $n=15.$ We want to select $10$ of those questions to answer, so we have $r=10.$\n\nTherefore, the number of ways to answer $10$ different questions is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{15}{C}_{10} & =\\frac{15!}{(15-10)!\\,10!} \\\\  & =\\frac{15!}{5!10!} \\\\  & =\\frac{15\\cdot 14\\cdot 13\\cdot 12\\cdot 11\\cdot \\cancel{10!}}{5!\\cancel{10!}} \\\\  & =\\frac{15\\cdot 14\\cdot 13\\cdot 12\\cdot 11}{5\\cdot 4\\cdot 3\\cdot 2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{360\\,360}{120} \\\\  & =3\\,003.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-5571/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d22726fc-8e6b-5e22-80c8-fbc2aa245217"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-5571"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-1784/selection/77464896c0404aca06ab8a1d74be701edf240734ab3ba5357d1ea3da368cd7e8" :answer/id #uuid "2b512be1-ddc2-57c0-adfc-dc032a1dbd78" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11\\,880" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-1784/selection/53a23f7c7e59c654cbb200db91f1b3b36b0bb586f917df4d2296ac2479c59d1a" :answer/id #uuid "573f9da9-197a-56d3-a76f-30f78e97fda7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "495" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-1784/selection/3aff3f3df25315995b2ef58b1d50bb64240f7651c87ff49eaf04d0aed9be6e2f" :answer/id #uuid "64fce1fa-a649-5f1c-962c-8e4b882f67af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "392" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-1784/selection/bfceda3d5a3e9713e61cb58c300caf53b568879d1da7422cafed8705fab22f08" :answer/id #uuid "d7b3bba9-a4f3-5f6c-9f1c-22893c13a49b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "22\\,480" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-1784/selection/4deb41f42f933c22a8010488db7c399dfd712c3e0c27fc8c8c93d500ada1d737" :answer/id #uuid "999314c4-a62c-535e-a927-3075860c7c12" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "692" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-1784/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "89cebde1-d009-5899-b4c9-9404895b0d3f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-1784/selection/53a23f7c7e59c654cbb200db91f1b3b36b0bb586f917df4d2296ac2479c59d1a" :answer-field/choices ["q-1784/selection/77464896c0404aca06ab8a1d74be701edf240734ab3ba5357d1ea3da368cd7e8" "q-1784/selection/53a23f7c7e59c654cbb200db91f1b3b36b0bb586f917df4d2296ac2479c59d1a" "q-1784/selection/3aff3f3df25315995b2ef58b1d50bb64240f7651c87ff49eaf04d0aed9be6e2f" "q-1784/selection/bfceda3d5a3e9713e61cb58c300caf53b568879d1da7422cafed8705fab22f08" "q-1784/selection/4deb41f42f933c22a8010488db7c399dfd712c3e0c27fc8c8c93d500ada1d737"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-1784" :question/id #uuid "c123f17c-f005-5ad1-89ae-b8a653b0f820" :question/math-academy-id "q-1784" :question/is-example false :question/problem "How many different ways can a team of four be made from a class of twelve students?" :question/worked-solution "In general, the number of combinations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{C}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $12$ students, so $n=12.$ We want to select $4$ of those students for the team, so we have $r=4.$\n\nTherefore, the number of different potential teams of four is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{12}{C}_{4} & =\\frac{12!}{(12-4)!\\,4!} \\\\  & =\\frac{12!}{8!4!} \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\cdot 11\\cdot 10\\cdot 9\\cdot \\cancel{8!}}{\\cancel{8!}4!} \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\cdot 11\\cdot 10\\cdot 9}{4\\cdot 3\\cdot 2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{11\\,880}{24} \\\\  & =495.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-1784/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d22726fc-8e6b-5e22-80c8-fbc2aa245217"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-1784"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-1781/selectio