5568" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Toria's friend holds a barrel of $150$ marbles in front of her, each with a slightly different size or color.  If she reaches in and grabs five of them, how many different groups of five marbles can Toria select?" :question/worked-solution "In general, the number of combinations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{C}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $150$ marbles, so $n=150.$ We want to select $5$ of those marbles from the bag, so we have $r=5.$\n\nTherefore, the number of different potential groups of five marbles is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{150}{C}_{5} & =\\frac{150!}{(150-5)!\\,5!} \\\\  & =\\frac{150!}{145!5!} \\\\  & =\\frac{150\\cdot 149\\cdot 148\\cdot 147\\cdot 146\\cdot \\cancel{145!}}{\\cancel{145!}5!} \\\\  & =\\frac{150\\cdot 149\\cdot 148\\cdot 147\\cdot 146}{5\\cdot 4\\cdot 3\\cdot 2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =591\\,600\\,030.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-5568/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d22726fc-8e6b-5e22-80c8-fbc2aa245217"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-5568"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
